PHASE 4: PINNED TAURI COMPRESSION PATH
--------------------------------------
tauri-cli 2.10.1 depends on tauri-bundler 2.8.1.

tauri-bundler 2.8.1, crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/updater_bundle.rs:
  bundle_update_macos locates the .app and names the updater source.app.tar.gz.
  create_tar constructs flate2::write::GzEncoder with Compression::default().
  create_tar_from_src constructs tar::Builder, sets follow_symlinks(false), and
  calls append_dir_all(src_dir.file_name(), src_dir).

Resolved implementation details from the installed cargo-tauri binary:
  tar 0.4.45
  flate2 1.1.9
  zlib-rs 0.6.3 (selected gzip/DEFLATE backend)

Compression::default() is level 6. GzEncoder::new uses a blank GzBuilder:
  FLG: 0 (no extra, filename, or comment)
  MTIME: 0
  XFL: 0 at level 6
  OS: 255

Official gzip first 32 bytes:
  1f 8b 08 00 00 00 00 00 00 ff ec bd 0b 7c 14 d5
  f5 38 7e 66 66 b3 3b 9b 04 42 c8 66 37 04 25 09

Tar generation does not select tar::HeaderMode::Deterministic, normalize file
metadata, or sort entries explicitly. append_dir_all reads filesystem entries;
the emitted archive therefore retains filesystem metadata and ordering as
observed by the pinned tar implementation. The controlled official tar has uid
501, gid 20 and per-entry mtimes from the source app tree.

PHASE 5: EXACT RECOMPRESSION CONTROL
------------------------------------
A deliberately wrong-backend control used flate2 1.1.9 with miniz_oxide 0.8.9:
  candidate size: 3936113
  candidate BLAKE3: 2080139b331ffe2a8c16d56960bcf4e7a2feb1bdac44b03e28174091f240c49e
  candidate SHA-256: b23498278ce08d76a9b4b25c175458c26273c35d9cee97f9ba0cbb5b90941715
  official size: 4070756
  first difference: zero-based byte 12 (inside DEFLATE data)
  gzip header bytes 0..9: identical
  result: NOT EQUIVALENT

The exact control used the installed cargo-tauri 2.10.1 binary as the pinned
compression oracle. The official tar was extracted with metadata preserved;
immediately before tauri-bundler's tar walk, source metadata was held equal to
the controlled tree. The raw tar emitted by the bundler was captured by
decompression and compared to official_new.tar before judging gzip output.

