SCIENTIFIC SCOPE
----------------
Measured: on this exact controlled v1.0.0 -> v1.0.1 pair, changing the patched
representation from official gzip bytes to their exact raw tar streams reduced
the zstd patch from 3884546 to 625269 bytes. Exact tar reconstruction, exact
pinned-bundler recompression, and verification by the existing signature all
passed.

Not established: general macOS ratios; performance on other changes, version
distances, platforms or bundler versions; the proposition that gzip generally
causes poor deltas; standalone raw-tar recompression stability across feature
resolution, compilers or platforms; production resource bounds and atomicity.
